{"timestamp": 1779339158.1928372, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 15, "data": {"caller": "player_3", "reason": "Diana reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "security", "victim_name": "Eve"}, {"room": "medbay", "victim_name": "Charlie"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779339158.193716, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 15, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779339167.091573, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I reported in security \u2014 Eve\u2019s body was right there when I arrived. My route was electrical -> medbay -> storage -> navigation -> security. I saw Frank in medbay very early, around tick 2. Later I saw Charlie in storage at ticks 6-7, and Charlie had entered storage from lower engine, so Charlie was definitely alive then. I didn\u2019t see anyone running away from security when I found Eve. Also it looks like Charlie is dead in medbay, but I did not personally find that body."}}
{"timestamp": 1779339186.239216, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I started security, went up weapons, then back through security toward nav/storage/medbay and ended cafeteria. I saw Eve early in weapons, then she went toward security; she was alive around there when I passed, but that was pretty early. I also saw Charlie in medbay late, around tick 13, and he was alive when I left for cafeteria. If Charlie\u2019s body is medbay, that happened right after I left or someone came in from storage/electrical. Diana\u2019s route sounds consistent with finding Eve, but I\u2019d really like to hear Frank and Alice\u2019s routes, especially Frank since Diana saw him medbay early and Charlie ended up there."}}
{"timestamp": 1779339208.770968, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "My route was cafeteria -> medbay -> electrical -> cafeteria -> weapons. I saw Diana in medbay around tick 2, and she should have seen me there too. After that I went to electrical, then back through cafeteria and ended in weapons. I did not see Charlie, Eve, Bob, or Alice at all this round, and I never went to security.\n\nSo for Charlie: I was only in medbay very early, and Bob says Charlie was alive in medbay around tick 13, which is much later than when I was there. If that\u2019s true, I don\u2019t think Diana\u2019s early sighting of me in medbay is relevant to Charlie\u2019s death.\n\nFor Eve: Diana reported in security, and Bob says he saw Eve early in weapons going toward security. That puts Bob near Eve early, but not enough by itself.\n\nRight now I think Diana\u2019s report and route sound pretty consistent. Bob is the only person so far who says he saw both victims, including Charlie alive very late, so that\u2019s worth noting, but I want to hear Alice\u2019s route before locking anything in."}}
{"timestamp": 1779339227.512012, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I don\u2019t have much hard info \u2014 my route was oxygen -> upper engine -> lower engine, and I didn\u2019t run into anyone at all, so I can\u2019t directly clear or accuse anyone.\n\nFrom what everyone said, Charlie being alive in medbay around tick 13 is the biggest point. If Charlie\u2019s body is in medbay, that makes Bob\u2019s timing really important because he\u2019s the last one claiming to see Charlie alive, and there\u2019s no one else confirming that. Frank was only medbay early, and Diana\u2019s medbay timing sounds early too, so they\u2019re less likely for Charlie unless their routes are false.\n\nFor Eve in security, Diana could technically self-report, but Bob also says Eve went toward security early after weapons. Bob is also the only person who says he saw both victims. I\u2019m not 100%, but Bob has the most connection to both deaths from the stories we have."}}
{"timestamp": 1779339239.0810869, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "My info is the same: I found Eve dead in security, and I did not see anyone leaving when I arrived. My route was electrical -> medbay -> storage -> navigation -> security. I saw Frank in medbay very early, around tick 2, and Charlie alive in storage at ticks 6-7 after he came in from lower engine.\n\nAfter hearing everyone, I agree the strongest suspicion is on Bob. He\u2019s the only one who places himself around both victims: Eve early near weapons/security, and Charlie alive very late in medbay. If Charlie\u2019s body is actually in medbay, Bob being the last person to see him alive is a big deal, especially with no one else confirming it.\n\nFrank and I both have early medbay timing, which doesn\u2019t line up with Charlie dying late unless Bob\u2019s timing is false. Alice has no hard info, but her route being isolated is at least not directly tied to either body. So unless Bob has a stronger explanation, I\u2019m leaning Bob here."}}
{"timestamp": 1779339269.027549, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I get why it looks bad because I\u2019m giving the late Charlie info, but that\u2019s exactly why I brought it up instead of hiding it. I\u2019m not claiming Charlie was dead when I left \u2014 I\u2019m saying he was alive in medbay at around tick 13 when I passed through to cafeteria.\n\nFor Eve, I saw her in weapons early and then security around tick 5, alive. I didn\u2019t report because there was no body when I passed. Diana is the one who found Eve in security later, and self-report is still possible there.\n\nAlso, Alice\u2019s route bothers me more now: she says oxygen -> upper -> lower and saw nobody, but Diana says Charlie came from lower engine into storage at ticks 6-7. If Alice was around lower engine, how does she not see Charlie at all? That\u2019s an actual mismatch, whereas my info is just \u201cI saw both victims alive.\u201d\n\nI don\u2019t think voting me just because I was honest about sightings is the right call. I\u2019d look harder at Alice\u2019s no-info route and Diana\u2019s self-report possibility before locking me."}}
{"timestamp": 1779339292.5768309, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I still think Bob is the best vote here.\n\nBob, I get that reporting sightings can be honest, but the problem is your route gives you opportunity on both bodies. You saw Eve in weapons/security early, and then you\u2019re also the only one placing Charlie alive in medbay very late. If Charlie died in medbay right after that, that points straight at you unless someone else admits being there late.\n\nThe Alice point isn\u2019t impossible, but it feels weaker to me. Alice could have missed Charlie depending on timing around lower engine/storage, and she\u2019s not tied to Eve at all. Diana self-report is technically possible for Eve, but then Charlie in medbay still needs explaining, and Diana\u2019s route doesn\u2019t line up with that as cleanly.\n\nMy own medbay timing was very early with Diana, so I don\u2019t think that explains Charlie. I\u2019m voting Bob unless the last speaker has something major."}}
{"timestamp": 1779339313.2106712, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "Bob, on the lower engine point: I never saw Charlie because timing can easily miss there. I went oxygen -> upper engine -> lower engine and saw nobody in my vision at any point. If Charlie had already gone from lower engine into storage around ticks 6-7, I could have been before or after that and just not crossed him. That\u2019s not really a contradiction, it\u2019s just two people moving through adjacent areas at different times.\n\nThe bigger issue is still opportunity. Diana found Eve in security, and Bob says he saw Eve around weapons/security earlier. Then Bob is also the only one claiming Charlie was alive very late in medbay, right before Charlie apparently died there. Frank and Diana both have early medbay timing that doesn\u2019t fit Charlie\u2019s death well. I have no connection to either body besides Bob trying to create one from a missed sighting.\n\nDiana self-report is technically possible for Eve, but it doesn\u2019t explain Charlie as cleanly. Bob explains both deaths the best from the routes. I\u2019m still leaning Bob."}}
